    "result_text": "The change is complete and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `Owner` model already had `customerCode` and `registrationDate` fields, and `POST /api/owners` is handled by `addOwner` in `OwnerRestControllerV1`. I added the audit emission:\n\n1. **Imported SLF4J** and declared a dedicated logger named `AUDIT`:\n   ```java\n   private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");\n   ```\n\n2. **Emitted the audit line** immediately after the successful `saveOwner(owner)` call (so the id is populated), carrying all three required values:\n   ```java\n   AUDIT.info(\"owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n       owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n   ```\n\nThe test `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` captures the `AUDIT` logger via a Logback `ListAppender` and asserts the message contains the owner id, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate` \u2014 it now passes, and the full suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\nNote the audit line is emitted only on the success path (after all validation/quota checks and the save), so rejected creates produce no audit entry, matching \"on successful create.\"",
